+# Bug Assessment: Category deletion removes products and breaks references
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: critical
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+A merchant deleted an old “Summer sale” category. Products belonging only to it disappeared, carts and orders containing them broke, and opening the deleted category by id returned a server error. DELETE `/api/v1/private/category/{id}` must delete only the category and descendants, preserve products and their data, remove only the deleted category memberships, preserve carts/orders, return 404 for deleted/missing categories, and make deleted-category product listings empty.
+
+## Symptom
+
+`CategoryServiceImpl.delete` deletes products when they have only one category, so category deletion destroys catalog entities referenced by carts and orders. The endpoint also can complete without deleting a missing category, while category reads can fail through stale or invalid category state instead of returning not found.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create a parent category with a child category and products assigned to the parent/child, including a product assigned to another category and a product assigned only to the deleted tree.
+2. Put those products in a cart and an order, then DELETE `/api/v1/private/category/{id}`.
+3. Verify products, stock, prices, carts, and orders remain usable; deleted categories and descendants return 404, are absent from category lists, and return no products; DELETE of an unknown id returns 404.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java:231-279` — deletion gathers descendants, then calls `productService.delete` for products with one category and removes only the root category explicitly.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java:360-368` — delete-by-id resolves the category through an unscoped `getById` path and delegates; its missing-category behavior must be guaranteed as a not-found response.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/category/CategoryApi.java:222-235` — public delete endpoint and response mapping.
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/product/Product.java:106-120` — product/category many-to-many association that must be updated without deleting products.
+- `sm-core-model/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/catalog/category/Category.java:55-62` — category descendants use `CascadeType.REMOVE`, so descendant deletion must be coordinated with product join rows.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. The deletion implementation explicitly treats a product with no remaining category as disposable and calls the full product deletion service, which removes catalog data needed by carts/orders. It also removes only the root category after collecting descendants, relying on cascade behavior without explicitly detaching product/category associations. The id lookup used by the delete facade is not store-scoped, which can produce incorrect behavior for missing or cross-store ids.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Make category deletion transactional and category-only. Resolve the requested category within the merchant store and throw `ResourceNotFoundException` when absent. Build the complete descendant set, load affected products, remove only those category objects from each product’s categories, and persist the product even when its category set becomes empty; never call `productService.delete`. Delete the root and descendants in a safe order (or use the existing cascade only after association cleanup), ensuring all descendant categories and their join rows are removed.
+
+Add focused service/API integration coverage for products with only deleted categories, products with retained categories, descendants, carts/orders, deleted-category reads/listings, and missing-id deletion.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/category/CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java`
+- Relevant core category tests if service-level coverage is added.
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Deleting a category tree preserves every affected product, stock, price, and non-deleted category memberships.
+- Deleting a category tree preserves cart and order reads/updates/checkout fixtures.
+- Deleted root/child categories return 404, disappear from lists, and yield no products; missing deletion returns 404.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Removing many-to-many links must happen before category rows are deleted to avoid foreign-key or stale persistence-context errors.
+- Products with no categories must remain valid and discoverable by SKU; changing product deletion semantics must not affect explicit product deletion.
+- Descendant traversal and deletion must remain restricted to the merchant store and avoid deleting another store’s category.
+- Full integration tests may require the project’s configured database and authenticated test fixture.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: None; the requested behavior is explicit.]
