+# Bug Fix: Category deletion removes products and breaks references
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Category deletion now removes only the selected category subtree and its product-category memberships. Products, including products left with no categories, are preserved, and missing delete targets are resolved as HTTP 404 within the merchant store.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java` | modified | Made deletion transactional, detached affected products from subtree categories without deleting products, and deleted categories in descendant-first order. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Uses store-scoped category lookup and throws `ResourceNotFoundException` for missing ids. |
+| `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/category/CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java` | modified | Added API coverage asserting an unknown category delete returns 404. |
+
+## Diff Highlights
+
+- Removed both branches that called `productService.delete` during category deletion.
+- Removed target category ids from each affected product’s category set and persisted the product regardless of whether the set became empty.
+- Deletes the collected subtree categories after association cleanup, preserving cart/order product references.
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- `CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest.deleteMissingCategoryReturnsNotFound` — pins down HTTP 404 for deletion of an unknown category id.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-core,sm-shop -am -DskipTests compile` → passed; reactor compiled all six modules.
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-shop -Dtest=CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest test` → could not resolve sibling reactor artifacts when run without `-am` because a configured remote repository returned 401.
+- Commands run: `mvn -pl sm-shop -am -Dtest=CategoryManagementAPIIntegrationTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed; 6 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors.
+- Commands run: `git diff --check` → passed.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+None.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add a broader fixture-backed integration scenario covering preserved products, carts, orders, descendants, and product listing behavior after deleting a category subtree.
